msgctxt "sessions_sign_in_required"
msgid "Sign in again to manage sessions."
msgstr "Reconnectez-vous pour gérer les sessions."

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the screen-reader action on a row that signs its session out (the row's visible control is the sign_out key). {device} is the row's device label, e.g. "Android" or "Unknown device".
msgctxt "sessions_sign_out_accessibility"
msgid "Sign out {}"
msgstr "Déconnecter {}"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the button at the bottom of the list that signs out every session except this one. Shown only when the list has this app's session and at least one other.
msgctxt "sessions_sign_out_all_others"
msgid "Sign out all other sessions"
msgstr "Déconnecter toutes les autres sessions"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): shown under the Sign out all other sessions button when signing the other sessions out failed.
msgctxt "sessions_sign_out_others_failed"
msgid "Couldn't sign out the other sessions. Try again."
msgstr "Impossible de déconnecter les autres sessions. Réessayez."

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions), row line 3: when the session was created, i.e. signed in. {date} is a localized date, e.g. "Oct 3". The sign-in method and the short ID follow: "Signed in Oct 3 · Google · ID 01a1f3c2".
msgctxt "sessions_signed_in"
msgid "Signed in {}"
msgstr "Connexion le {}"

#. Shown when this app was signed out because another device signed its session out on the Sessions screen (Account > Sessions). Only when the app knows that was the cause; otherwise the generic sign-in-required wording applies.
msgctxt "sessions_signed_out_remotely"
msgid "This session was signed out from another device."
msgstr "Cette session a été déconnectée depuis un autre appareil."

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): shown on a row, or on the Sign out all other sessions button, while its sign-out is pending. The control stays disabled meanwhile.
msgctxt "sessions_signing_out"
msgid "Signing out…"
msgstr "Déconnexion…"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the tag on the row of the session this app is signed in with (always the first row).
msgctxt "sessions_this_session"
msgid "This session"
msgstr "Cette session"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): the screen's title, and the label of the Account row after Profile that opens it. The screen lists the account's signed-in sessions, one per signed-in app or device, and signs them out.
msgctxt "sessions_title"
msgid "Sessions"
msgstr "Sessions"

#. Sessions screen (Account > Sessions): shown in place of the list when the server does not support session management yet.
msgctxt "sessions_unsupported"
