#. Label for the terms and conditions acceptance checkbox.
#. It should read like "I agree to URnetwork's <link>Terms and Services</link> and <link>Privacy Policy</link>"
#. 
#. The {terms_start} and {terms_end} markers wrap the "Terms and Services" text.
#. The {privacy_start} and {privacy_end} markers wrap the "Privacy Policy" text.
#. 
#. Platform-specific rendering:
#. - Web: Replace {terms_start} with <a href="/terms">, {terms_end} with </a>, etc.
#. - iOS: Use these markers to identify ranges for NSAttributedString link attributes
#. - Android: Use these markers to identify ranges for ClickableSpan
#. 
msgctxt "terms_checkbox"
msgid "I agree to URnetwork's {terms_start}Terms and Services{terms_end} and {privacy_start}Privacy Policy{privacy_end}"
msgstr "J'accepte les {terms_start}Conditions d'utilisation{terms_end} et la {privacy_start}Politique de confidentialité{privacy_end} d'URnetwork"

#. Get Pro screen: debug button that replays the Pro celebration animation.
msgctxt "test_animation"
msgid "Test animation"
msgstr "Tester l'animation"

#. Used in Shared/Views/PurchaseSuccessView.swift.
msgctxt "thanks_for_building_the_new_internet_with_us"
msgid "Thanks for building the new internet with us"
msgstr "Merci de construire le nouvel internet avec nous"

#. Confirmation shown after feedback is sent.
msgctxt "thanks_for_the_feedback"
msgid "Thanks for the feedback!"
msgstr "Merci pour votre retour !"

#. Shown inline in the upgrade flow when a StoreKit purchase attempt throws (Shared/ViewModels/AppStoreSubscriptionManager.swift). Every purchase failure is shown to the user — a payment error they cannot see is one they will hit again. User cancellation is not an error and never shows this.
msgctxt "the_purchase_could_not_be_completed"
msgid "The purchase could not be completed. Please try again."
msgstr "L’achat n’a pas pu aboutir. Réessayez."

