#. Shown inline in the upgrade flow when the server's verify answer for a purchase's transaction JWS is terminal `invalid` — the proof will never verify. The transaction is still finished so StoreKit stops redelivering it; this message is how the failure reaches the user instead of a silent success (Shared/ViewModels/AppStoreSubscriptionManager.swift). Apple sibling of purchase_could_not_be_verified (android).
msgctxt "this_purchase_couldn_t_be_verified"
msgid "This purchase couldn't be verified with the App Store, so it can't be applied to your account. If you were charged and your plan doesn't update, please contact support."
msgstr "Cet achat n’a pas pu être vérifié auprès de l’App Store, il ne peut donc pas être appliqué à votre compte. Si vous avez été débité et que votre forfait ne se met pas à jour, contactez l’assistance."

